/-!
# The plus-four branch of the almost-special argument

This entry exports the literal G.2.2 replacement hypotheses, the orthogonal
model and generation calculation, the odd-residual central-kernel proof of
S=WWᵍ, and the relative normal series and commutator bound in G.2.6(1–4).
The canonical S/S₂ action has two actual factor-specific natural-module
sums, complementary marked images and zero common odd fixed space.

The literal Chapter 15 application constructs its P/V action after the
central middle-layer collapse and identifies the residual-factor summands.
These results discharge all preceding structural and representation inputs.
The equality of the two natural-module multiplicities remains unresolved;
the full-clause adapters explicitly retain it. This entry therefore does
not claim the full printed G.2.6 or 15.3.54.

Source: Aschbacher–Smith, G.2.6, printed p.336, and 15.3.54, p.1146.
-/
